{{> menu active="about"}}

<header class="box is-3 has-text-centered">
  <h3 class="title">
    Weathertop
  </h3>
  <h4 class = "subtitle">
    Your Weather, Your Way
  </h4>
</header>
<div class="box">
  <p>
    Weathertop is a student project for SETU Waterford HDip in computer science designed to simulate a weather monitoring app.
    This App is not designed for commercial use.
  </p>
  <h4 class = "subtitle mb-1 mt-4">
    Using the App
  </h4>
  <p>
    Weathertop allows users to create an account using a login and password. Upon registering and signing in, users are able to add weather stations
    based on real locations. Within these stations, users can manually add time stamped weather readings to their station(s) or autogenerate a 
    reading in realtime using the Openweather API. A summary panel can be found both within individual station pages or on the users dashboard. 
    This provides a summary of all reports committed to the database, including current figures and maximum and minimum values. These are supported by
    graphics to visualise these trends over time. Users have the ability to edit or delete reports as required. Users can also delete weather stations
    from their dashboard, also deleting all reports associated with that station from the database. 
  </p>
  <h4 class ="subtitle mb-1 mt-4">
    Notes on metrics
  </h4>
  <p>
  Wind description seen on summary panels is defined from wind speed in knots using the <a href ="https://www.weather.gov/mfl/beaufort">Beufort Wind Scale</a>
  . Feels like temperature within these panels represents the <a href = "https://www.omnicalculator.com/other/wind-chill">wind chill temperature</a> using the 
  formula T_wc = 13.12 + 0.6215 * temperature * (0.3965 * temperature - 11.37) * wind speed^0.16.
  </p>
  <h4 class = "subtitle mb-1 mt-4">
  Upcoming features
  </h4>
  <p>
    <ul>
      <li>Map Markers for weather map</li>
    </ul>
  </p>
